"  So threshold is ~ 10^{log10_threshold:.0f}\")\nprint()\n\n# But this is the worst case. When x is also large, the S term helps\n# The R-coeff = -298*c^4*(1+t)^4 - c^2*(1+t)^2*(1+x)^2 + 299*(1+x)^4\n# When x >> c*t: R-coeff ~ 299*(1+x)^4 > 0, so R-term is POSITIVE -> no problem\n# When c*t >> x: R-coeff ~ -298*c^4*(1+t)^4, so we need poly >> R * |R-coeff|\n\n# The most dangerous case: x = 0 (or small), t large\n# Numerator(x=0) = 597502500*c^4*(1+t)^4 + 995000*c^2*(1+t)^2 + 597502500\n#                 + (1+t)^{1/100}*[-298*c^4*(1+t)^4 - c^2*(1+t)^2 + 299]\n# For large t with x=0:\n# ~ c^4*t^4*(597502500 - 298*t^{1/100}) + lower order terms\n# Turns negative when t^{1/100} ~ 2004707, i.e., t ~ 2004707^100 ~ 10^630\n\nprint(\"WORST CASE (x=0, large t):\")\nprint(f\"  L2 turns negative around t ~ 10^{log10_threshold:.0f}\")\nprint()\nprint(\"This is an astronomically large threshold, but L2 is NOT globally non-negative.\")\nprint(\"L2 EVENTUALLY becomes negative for sufficiently large t (or large (1+t)(1+x)).\")\nprint()\n\n# However, the engine only samples x in [0,50], t in [0,10], which is well within the safe zone\n# Let's verify at larger values\n\n# Let me also check: what does the candidate log claim?\n# \"Verified with mpmath arbitrary precision: L2 > 0 at x = 10^{1000}, t = 10^{500}, c = 10^{500}\"\n# But our analysis shows failure at t ~ 10^630 with x=0... let me recheck\n\n# At x=0, t large: need 597502500 > 298*(1+t)^{1/100}\n# (1+t)^{1/100} < 2004706.7... \n# t^{1/100} < 2004707 => t < 2004707^100\n# log10(2004707) = 6.302...\n# t < 10^{630.2}\n\n# The candidate says \"verified at t = 10^500\" which is BELOW the threshold!\n# t = 10^500 < 10^630, so L2 > 0 there as expected.\n\n# But at t = 10^{631}, x = 0, L2 would be negative.\n\nprint(\"CRITICAL FINDING:\")\nprint(f\"  At x=0, t=10^631, c=1: L2 < 0 (threshold ~ 10^630)\")\nprint(f\"  The candidate log's mpmath tests at t=10^500 are below this threshold\")\nprint(f\"  L2 is NOT globally non-negative f